cts/agent-runner/worktrees/age-pid-sidecar/planning/s11-gate/evidence/source-commits.log | 1689 | 641c220ae12a | Read because the transport-rotation proof method references this evidence log. |\n14: \n15: ## Proof-plan parse\n16: | Field | Present | Evidence |\n17: |---|---:|---|\n18: | `## Proof plan` | Yes | `proposal.md:9` exact heading. |\n19: | `Runtime claim` | Yes | Ten runtime-claim entries at `proposal.md:13`, `:19`, `:25`, `:31`, `:37`, `:43`, `:49`, `:55`, `:61`, `:67`. |\n20: | `Proof method` | Yes | Ten proof-method entries at `proposal.md:15`, `:21`, `:27`, `:33`, `:39`, `:45`, `:51`, `:57`, `:63`, `:69`. |\n21: | `Evidence-class match` | Yes | Ten evidence-class-match entries at `proposal.md:17`, `:23`, `:29`, `:35`, `:41`, `:47`, `:53`, `:59`, `:65`, `:71`. |\n22: | Self-certification only | No | The plan names concrete CLI integration tests, provider protocol capture tests, live runtime artifacts, sidecar DB artifacts, source schema files, and scoped compatibility tests rather than treating the plan text itself as validation. |\n23: \n24: ## Findings\n25: | Finding ID | Severity | Runtime claim | Proof plan ref | Proof method | Proxy class | Required runtime artifact | Evidence refs | Blocks pipeline |\n26: |---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n27: | None | None | No proof-risk finding. | N/A | N/A | N/A | N/A | N/A | No |\n28: \n29: ## Evidence-class decision\n30: \n31: The proof-plan structure is complete. Each claim has a runtime claim, proof method, and evidence-class match statement.\n32: \n33: The external launch, wake, delivery-confirmation, and retry claims at `proposal.md:13-29` are runtime/sidecar-path claims. Their proof methods bind to CLI/external-provider integration tests that launch the runner through the external provider fixture, assert sidecar pid-identity/mailbox state, and cover spawn, no-turn, submitted-turn marker, mismatch, failure, rate-limit, claim release, and retry paths. The contract declares `src-tauri/tests/s11_external_provider_wake.rs` as the CLI launch/notify/wake/resume integration surface and declares `crates/oulipoly-state/src/mailbox.rs` as the intrinsic sidecar mailbox delivery state surface, so the evidence class matches the claim rather than only a detached proxy.\n34: \n35: The external-provider transport rotation claim at `proposal.md:31-35` is a runtime dispatch/pool-selection claim. Its proof method uses the `age246_external_transport_rotation` runtime integration fixture to configure multiple provider accounts, force timeout or unavailable classes, assert retry onto the next account, and assert all-slow bounded terminal behavior. That is matching runtime integration evidence for the claimed rotation boundary.\n36: \n37: The provider policy/launch shaping claim at `proposal.md:37-41` targets request and environment construction at the runner/provider boundary. The proof method uses provider-client/executor integration fixtures that capture the actual policy and launch protocol requests, settings identity, launch shape, host linkage env, account auth context, secret filtering, and rejection branch. Because the claim is about protocol request shape and environment boundary, fixture-captured protocol evidence is the matching evidence class, not a proxy mismatch.\n38: \n39: The detached wake registry/session-root claim at `proposal.md:43-47` is bound to CLI/external-provider integration with isolated model/config/data roots and an ingested-session fallback case. That exercises the resume path's model root and session source behavior named by the claim.\n40: \n41: The S10 compatibility claim at `proposal.md:49-53` is mixed evidence with explicit scoping. Deterministic CLI integration tests remain the binding external launch/resume compatibility proof, while live `/tmp/s10-e2e/final*.log` smoke files are scoped only to external launch success. The proposal explicitly states that unavailable `S10-FINAL-OK` / `S10-RESUME-OK` live logs are not substituted for the shipped resume tests, which avoids the specific proxy substitution risk called out by the user.\n42: \n43: The xhigh external route claim at `proposal.md:55-59` is runtime-artifact-bound and is matched to retained live runtime task output that records the external route marker and successful status. The live S11 wake-delivery claim at `proposal.md:61-65` is also runtime-artifact-bound and is matched to argv logs, sidecar `pid-identity.db`, invocation result, exported session, and workload marker files. These are direct runtime/sidecar artifacts for the behavior asserted.\n44: \n45: The no-`state.db` migration claim at `proposal.md:67-71` is a source/schema invariant claim, not a claim that a new production migration executes. The proof method names touched-file inventory, schema and migration source files, and state/mailbox tests showing the behavior uses existing session-turn reads and existing sidecar mailbox columns. The contract also states that no `state.db` schema migration is declared or required, which matches this evidence class.\n46: \n47: ## Residual ambiguity / stop-condition notes\n48: \n49: No stop condition fired. The proposal-relative evidence paths `planning/s11-gate/evidence/runtime-tests.log`, `planning/s11-gate/evidence/live-smoke.md`, and `planning/s11-gate/evidence/source-commits.log` did not exist under the supplied `/tmp/s11-gate-worktree-a1a3ca1` root, but the caller supplied absolute evidence-summary paths under `/home/nes/projects/agent-runner/worktrees/age-pid-sidecar/`, and those summaries were readable. This does not create a proof-risk mismatch because the proof plan directly names concrete shipped tests, runtime command summaries, and live artifact classes, and this operator scores evidence-class matching rather than regenerating evidence.\n50: \n51: LOW\n\n(End of file - total 51 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Proof-risk audit report\n\n## Inputs read\n| Input | Path or value | Size | SHA excerpt | Notes |\n|---|---|---:|---|---|